# Bab 6 — REST: requests show verbs, versioned routes, bodies, credentials, and expected outcomes.
# Bab 11 — each domain uses its own synthetic user's token; wrong-role behavior is intentional.
# Bab 16 — this file is the interactive companion to the OpenAPI/Swagger contract.
#
# Setup before running protected/resource requests:
# 1. Change host to http://localhost:8080 when using Docker Compose.
# 2. Change runId to a unique 1-16 character suffix for every walkthrough.
# 3. Run the relevant login request.
# 4. Copy accessToken/refreshToken into the matching variables below.
# 5. Copy returned resource IDs into patientId, assetId, customerId, or accountId.
#
# The explicit copy steps keep this file portable across HTTP clients; response-handler syntax differs by editor.
@host = http://localhost:5056
@runId = change-me-001
@healthcareToken = paste-healthcare-access-token-here
@healthcareRefreshToken = paste-healthcare-refresh-token-here
@industrialToken = paste-industrial-access-token-here
@logisticsToken = paste-logistics-access-token-here
@bankingToken = paste-banking-access-token-here
@patientId = paste-patient-id-here
@assetId = paste-asset-id-here
@customerId = paste-customer-id-here
@accountId = paste-account-id-here

### Host: OpenAPI is available in Development — expect 200
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json
Accept: application/json

### Auth: no bearer token — expect 401
GET {{host}}/api/v1/auth/me

### Auth setup: login as healthcare.demo — expect 200; copy accessToken and refreshToken
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "healthcare.demo",
  "password": "HealthDemo!123"
}

### Auth: inspect healthcare identity — expect 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{healthcareToken}}

### Authorization: healthcare policy permits healthcare.demo — expect 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/auth/probes/healthcare
Authorization: Bearer {{healthcareToken}}

### Authorization: banking-transfer policy rejects healthcare.demo — expect 403
GET {{host}}/api/v1/auth/probes/banking-transfer
Authorization: Bearer {{healthcareToken}}

### Validation: required patient fields are absent — expect 400 validation_failed
POST {{host}}/api/v1/healthcare/patients
Authorization: Bearer {{healthcareToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Healthcare setup: create a unique synthetic patient — expect 201; copy id to patientId
POST {{host}}/api/v1/healthcare/patients
Authorization: Bearer {{healthcareToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "medicalRecordNumber": "MRN-HTTP-{{runId}}",
  "displayName": "Synthetic Patient HTTP",
  "birthDate": "1988-05-10"
}

### Domain conflict: repeat the same medical record number — expect 409 patient_already_exists
POST {{host}}/api/v1/healthcare/patients
Authorization: Bearer {{healthcareToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "medicalRecordNumber": "MRN-HTTP-{{runId}}",
  "displayName": "Duplicate Synthetic Patient",
  "birthDate": "1988-05-10"
}

### Persistence: retrieve the created patient — expect 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/healthcare/patients/{{patientId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{healthcareToken}}
X-Correlation-Id: http-healthcare-{{runId}}

### Domain invariant: an appointment cannot be in the past — expect 422
POST {{host}}/api/v1/healthcare/patients/{{patientId}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{healthcareToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "startsAtUtc": "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "provider": "Synthetic Provider"
}

### Token lifecycle: rotate the healthcare refresh token — expect 200; replace both token variables
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{healthcareRefreshToken}}"
}

### Token lifecycle: revoke the current healthcare refresh token — expect 204
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/revoke
Authorization: Bearer {{healthcareToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{healthcareRefreshToken}}"
}

### Industrial setup: login — expect 200; copy accessToken to industrialToken
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "industrial.demo",
  "password": "IndustrialDemo!123"
}

### Industrial setup: create a unique synthetic asset — expect 201; copy id to assetId
POST {{host}}/api/v1/industrial/assets
Authorization: Bearer {{industrialToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetCode": "ASSET-HTTP-{{runId}}",
  "displayName": "Synthetic Press HTTP"
}

### Industrial: record telemetry and invalidate application cache — expect 202
POST {{host}}/api/v1/industrial/assets/{{assetId}}/telemetry
Authorization: Bearer {{industrialToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "value": 42,
  "unit": "percent"
}

### Industrial: read telemetry with gzip accepted — expect 200 and Content-Encoding: gzip
GET {{host}}/api/v1/industrial/assets/{{assetId}}/telemetry
Authorization: Bearer {{industrialToken}}
Accept-Encoding: gzip

### Logistics setup: login — expect 200; copy accessToken to logisticsToken
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "logistics.demo",
  "password": "LogisticsDemo!123"
}

### Logistics setup: create a unique shipment — expect 201
POST {{host}}/api/v1/logistics/shipments
Authorization: Bearer {{logisticsToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "trackingNumber": "SHIP-HTTP-{{runId}}",
  "origin": "Synthetic Origin",
  "destination": "Synthetic Destination"
}

### Logistics: retrieve the created shipment — expect 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/logistics/shipments/SHIP-HTTP-{{runId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{logisticsToken}}

### Banking setup: login — expect 200; copy accessToken to bankingToken
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "banking.demo",
  "password": "BankingDemo!123"
}

### Banking setup: create a unique synthetic customer — expect 201; copy id to customerId
POST {{host}}/api/v1/banking/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{bankingToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerReference": "CUSTOMER-HTTP-{{runId}}",
  "displayName": "Synthetic Customer HTTP"
}

### Banking setup: create an account — expect 201; copy id to accountId
POST {{host}}/api/v1/banking/customers/{{customerId}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{bankingToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountReference": "ACCOUNT-HTTP-{{runId}}",
  "currency": "SIM",
  "initialBalanceMinor": 10000
}

### Banking: inspect synthetic transactions — expect 200 and an empty array before transfers
GET {{host}}/api/v1/banking/accounts/{{accountId}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{bankingToken}}
Accept-Encoding: gzip
